<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

  Merged by the Tauri CLI into the Mac bundle's Contents/Info.plist: Tauri 2 picks up an
  Info.plist that sits next to tauri.conf.json (documented on tauri-utils
  MacConfig::info_plist and in Tauri's "macOS Application Bundle" guide; tauri-codegen
  embeds the same file in development builds).

  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription (WO2 section 4.8, trap 3): without it macOS ends the app
  the first time it touches the microphone. macOS shows this sentence in its own permission
  prompt, after the app's own explanation (jk_recorder::input::MIC_PERMISSION_EXPLANATION).
  It must equal jk_recorder::input::MACOS_MIC_USAGE_DESCRIPTION (a jk-recorder test checks
  it), and scripts/build-mac.sh checks that the built bundle carries it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Open Mic listens to your microphone only while practice mode is open, to show and grade the pitch you sing. The sound is analysed in memory on this Mac and is never recorded, saved or sent anywhere.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
